    "collapsible_content_fPD3dL": {
      "type": "collapsible-content",
      "blocks": {
        "collapsible_row_VbgArw": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What is Onda Origins Cafe & Roastery known for?",
            "icon": "question_mark",
            "row_content": "<p>Onda Origins Cafe & Roastery is known for its farmer-first coffee sourcing model, where growers are paid above market rates and receive ongoing revenue sharing. It also stands out as a community-focused cafe and micro roastery in South Seattle that combines high-quality specialty coffee with ethical sourcing practices.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_8UigYw": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Where is Onda Origins Cafe & Roastery located?",
            "icon": "question_mark",
            "row_content": "<p>Onda Origins Cafe & Roastery is located in the Hillman City neighborhood of South Seattle, just south of Columbia City on Rainier Ave. The cafe serves as both a specialty roastery and a neighborhood gathering space.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_9QHUid": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Is there free parking?",
            "icon": "question_mark",
            "row_content": "<p>Yes - there's free 2-hour parking all along Rainier Ave., and plenty of neighborhood parking along Findlay and surrounding neighborhood streets. It's also a beautiful neighborhood to go for a walk in with coffee in hand!</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_AwMHNt": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Who owns Onda Origins Cafe & Roastery?",
            "icon": "question_mark",
            "row_content": "<p>Onda Origins was founded by brothers Paul and Scott Tupper, who created the business to improve transparency and fairness in the global coffee supply chain. Learn more <a href=\"/pages/onda-origins-coffee-story-seattle\" title=\"Our Story\"><em><strong>here.</strong></em></a></p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_iXQLyc": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How is Onda Origins Cafe & Roastery different from other coffee shops?",
            "icon": "question_mark",
            "row_content": "<p>Unlike traditional coffee shops, Onda Origins uses a direct trade and profit-sharing model with coffee farmers. This means producers benefit not just from initial sales, but also from the long-term success of the coffee, making it more sustainable and equitable at every level. Learn more <a href=\"/pages/howweredifferent\" title=\"How We're Different\"><em><strong>here.</strong></em></a></p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_zLhHwk": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Does Onda Origins Cafe & Roastery support the local community?",
            "icon": "question_mark",
            "row_content": "<p>Yes, Onda Origins is deeply involved in the local community. They often host events, art collaborations, and pop-up markets, and even supported local community members and farmers during COVID-19 by turning the cafe into a small marketplace.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        }
      },
